From: Serj Targarien <xergy10@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: report the RGB20SX sticks and FN the standard way

The RGB20SX shares the RK2023's device tree, whose stick Y axes run the other
way on this board: pushing either stick up reports a larger value, where
input devices report up as smaller (probed: both sticks rest near 520 and
read 1004-1023 pushed up). Flip both Y ranges; the adc-joystick driver
inverts an axis whose range runs high to low and still reports 15-1023.

Both polled devices, the sticks and the FN key, are read every 60 ms, which
lags a stick or a held FN by up to a frame and a half at 60 Hz. Poll them
every 10 ms, so no reader has to change it at run time.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-powkiddy-rgb20sx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-powkiddy-rgb20sx.dts
@@ -107,3 +107,23 @@
 	num-interpolated-steps = <255>;
 	default-brightness-level = <77>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * basesq: the sticks the right way up (the RK2023's Y axes run upward on the RGB20SX;
+ * X is right), and the sticks and FN polled every 10 ms instead of 60.
+ */
+&{/adc-joystick} {
+	poll-interval = <10>;
+};
+
+&{/adc-joystick/axis@2} {
+	abs-range = <1023 15>;
+};
+
+&{/adc-joystick/axis@3} {
+	abs-range = <15 1023>;
+};
+
+&adc_keys {
+	poll-interval = <10>;
+};
